     "My organisation would like to make the interactive data visualization ( with Shiny web application) available to the public via its website.  According to the following link <span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">, </span><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><a href=\"http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#deployment-web\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/%23deployment-web&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409164164000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0ofl8zgV4qvSQ6cFEuvyO3\">http://rstudio.github.io/shiny/tutorial/#deployment-web</a> , Shiny can only work with Linux server.  </span>Our server is <a href=\"http://ASP.NET\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://ASP.NET&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792409164165000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1-3N9v4ueKPnnbYTaaNq7C\">ASP.NET</a>. <span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">Is that a way to make Shiny compatible to that platform?</span><div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"><br></span></font></div><div><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Thanks<br></span></font><div><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"><br></span></div></div>"
